SUPERSEDED — DO NOT RUN.

This file previously held a draft of the stage-2 listening changes. It has been
applied, and then CORRECTED, via proper migrations:

  supabase/migrations/20260817104100_stage2_listening_audio_coupled.sql
  supabase/migrations/20260817161500_fix_fire_safety_regression.sql

The draft contained two defects that the migrations above fix:

  1. `where id like '64368a14%'` on a uuid column — invalid without a ::text cast,
     so it aborted mid-transaction.
  2. It edited question 6d3a5ad1 as though it were a STANDALONE listening item.
     It is passage-linked (passage d6b0e8b0), so the spoken script is the PASSAGE
     body, not the question's prompt_text. Running it overwrote a question stem
     and replaced an option set with one that no longer contained its own
     correct_answer, making the item unanswerable.

Rule learned: check `passage_id` before editing any listening question, and run
  select id from public.questions where type='mcq' and not (options ? correct_answer);
after every content migration.
